---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import ProvidersDirectory from '../../components/ProvidersDirectory.astro';
import { resolvePath } from '../../utils/paths.js';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Supported Providers Directory"
  description="Catalog of 84+ supported ATS platforms, job boards, and aggregators with extraction modes."
  currentPath={resolvePath('/docs/providers/')}
  category="Ecosystem"
>
  <h1>Supported Job Boards & ATS Providers</h1>
  <p>
    JobFoundry supports over 84 job boards, Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS), and career portals. All extractions are executed locally within your browser using DOM scrapers and JSON-LD structured schemas.
  </p>

  <div class="doc-callout">
    <div class="callout-title">
      <span>◈</span>
      <span>Request a New Provider</span>
    </div>
    <p>
      Don't see a job board or enterprise ATS you frequent? Submit a provider request via our <a href={resolvePath('/feedback/')}>Feedback Portal</a> or file an issue on GitHub with a sample job posting URL.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Provider Directory (84+)</h2>
  <p>
    Use the search bar or category filters below to check coverage and extraction mechanics for any platform:
  </p>

  <ProvidersDirectory />

  <h2>How Providers Work Under the Hood</h2>
  <p>
    Each provider extractor lives in <code>extension/src/extractors/</code> and exports a standard interface:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`// Interface: ProviderExtractor
interface ProviderExtractor {
  matches(url: URL): boolean;
  extract(document: Document): ExtractedJobPayload | null;
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    When you open a job listing, the extension checks URL match patterns. If a known provider matches, it parses the document immediately. If an unrecognized site contains standard <code>schema.org/JobPosting</code> JSON-LD, the generic fallback extractor automatically captures it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contributing a New Extractor</h2>
  <p>
    Adding support for a new job board takes fewer than 30 lines of code. Read our <a href="https://github.com/deadrat-in/JobFoundry/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Contributing Guide</a> to submit a pull request!
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
